diff --git a/SETUP-PULL.md b/SETUP-PULL.md
index 27adb62..f58bd7b 100644
--- a/SETUP-PULL.md
+++ b/SETUP-PULL.md
@@ -133,6 +133,12 @@ With `RDGEN_PUBLISH_DEFAULT` set (no, hidden or published), the form asks whethe
 
 CortenDesk's `/downloads` page needs no login, and a client with a preset permanent password carries that password. rdgen therefore refuses "published" for such a client, and the pending list reports it as hidden. In the RustDesk LXC the job is `rdgen-publish`, which runs every minute.
 
+### Recent builds and share links
+
+`/builds` (linked from the form) lists the builds of the last `RDGEN_RETENTION_DAYS` with their files and status. For a finished build it makes a **share link**: `/share/<token>` shows the build's files and needs no login, so you can send a client to someone without putting it on a public page. The token is 32 random bytes. A link expires after 1, 7 or 30 days, and never later than the build itself; you can delete it sooner. Each link counts its downloads.
+
+Links point at `RDGEN_SHARE_BASE` when it is set (e.g. `https://console.example.com/share`). Otherwise they point at rdgen itself, which is normally reachable on the LAN only. A reverse proxy on that public host has to pass exactly `/share/<43 characters>` and `/share/<43 characters>/<file>` to rdgen, GET only, and nothing else. The RustDesk LXC's console does that.
+
 CortenDesk does not read the client's `preset-*` keys, so rdgen's address-book, strategy and device-group presets have no effect there. Clients from rdgen at version 1.4.1 or later need an hbbs with KeyExchange; cortendesk-server has it.
 
 ## 3. Updates
@@ -176,6 +182,7 @@ The patches fix these upstream problems (the commit messages have the details):
 They do not change these:
 - GitHub sees the decrypted config (server, key, preset password) in runner memory and in the built binaries while a build runs. Values are masked in logs.
 - The preset password is only base64-encoded in every client (`custom_.txt`), so treat it as low-grade.
+- Anyone who holds a share link can download that build until the link expires or is deleted, including a preset password inside it.
 - Unsigned Windows builds trigger SmartScreen and antivirus warnings.
 - The UI loads Font Awesome from cdnjs and a Google font (upstream `generator.html`), which your browser fetches.
 - Failed runs and their logs stay in your private repository for 48 hours. They contain masked values and ciphertext.
